.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt QCABTFW 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qcabtfw
.Nd load firmware for Qualcomm Atheros QCA61x4 Bluetooth USB devices
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl DI
.Fl d Ar device_name
.Op Fl f Ar firmware_path
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility downloads firmware to the specified
.Xr ugen 4
device.
.Pp
This utility will
.Em only
work with Qualcomm Atheros QCA61x4
.Pq Dq ROME
based Bluetooth USB devices, such as the Bluetooth half of the QCA6174
wireless adaptor.
The identification is based on the USB vendor ID/product ID pair.
.Pp
These devices start from a ROM firmware and need two files before they
can be used: a rampatch,
.Pa rampatch_usb_XXXXXXXX.bin ,
and an NVM configuration,
.Pa nvm_usb_XXXXXXXX.bin ,
where
.Ar XXXXXXXX
is the ROM version reported by the device.
Both files are distributed in the
.Pa qca
directory of the linux-firmware collection.
.Pp
The
.Nm
utility queries the device to find out which parts are missing, downloads
them and then resets the device so that
.Xr ng_ubt 4
attaches to it.
It is normally started by
.Xr devd 8
when the device is plugged in.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl D
Enable verbose debugging.
.It Fl d Ar device_name
Specify
.Xr ugen 4
device name.
.It Fl f Ar firmware_path
Specify the directory containing the firmware files.
The default is
.Pa /usr/share/firmware/qcabt .
.It Fl h
Display usage message and exit.
.It Fl I
Enable informational debugging.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/share/qcabt-firmware" -compact
.It Pa /etc/devd/qcabtfw.conf
.Xr devd 8
rules that run
.Nm
on device attach.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/qcabt-firmware
Firmware directory used by the
.Xr devd 8
rules.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libusb 3 ,
.Xr ng_ubt 4 ,
.Xr ugen 4 ,
.Xr devd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
